            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0146" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363 Barco/470</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-11">March 11, 1931</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 223</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your telegram
                    No. 29 of March 4, 6.00 p.m., reporting the signing of a contract for the
                    settlement of the Barco Concession controversy by representatives of the South
                    American Gulf Oil Company and the Colombian authorities. The Department has
                    noted with great satisfaction the skill, tact and good judgment which you have
                    exercised in extending your informal good offices to assist the private American
                    interests involved and the Colombian Government to arrive at a mutually
                    satisfactory settlement of this long pending and difficult question, and desires
                    to commend you upon the successful termination of the controversy.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
